Z||000013||William||03-10-2001||01:33 AM||||Guy's, thank you for the encourging words! I got luke warm comments from family and friends. I knew it would take fiero fans to really appreciate the project. It really was alot of work and I'm glad it's over. In my earlier post, I left out alot of the little details and problems. Anyone remember my post about the razor knife slash across my chest? hehe<P>MrPBody : The wheel feels kinda small in hands put we shall see.<P>Wolfhound: I have thought about doing the console in black but thats still iffy.<P>voyagerspe: Black laquer paint, 1500 grit sandpaper, buffing compound, and many <BR>hours!!!!<P>rodmcneill: Your sure called that one!! At this point I'm scared to even sit in the car. With all the light colored leather and carpet, it's going to be really tough to keep it mint. I was blind to this fact until just after I finshed it and was forced to wash the bottoms of my shoes before I sat in the car...   :-)<P><BR>||||reg||1
